</span>) or <strong>https://</strong> means you’ve safely connected to the .gov website. Share
sensitive information only on official, secure websites.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section><div class=usa-overlay></div><header class="usa-header usa-header--extended usgs-header" role=banner><div class=usgs-header-container><div class=usa-navbar><div class=usa-logo id=extended-logo><a href=https://www.usgs.gov><img alt="USGS Home" src=/blog/wdfn-viz/img/USGS_logo.svg></a></div><button type=button class=usa-menu-btn>Menu</button></div></div><nav role=navigation class=usa-nav><div class=usa-nav__inner><button type=button class=usa-nav__close><img src=/blog/wdfn-viz/img/usa-icons/close.svg alt=close></button><ul class="usa-nav__primary usa-accordion"><li class=usa-nav__primary-item><a class=usa-nav__link href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/>Water Data Blog</a></li><li class=usa-nav__primary-item><a class=usa-nav__link href=/blog/introduction><span>About</span></a></li><li class=usa-nav__primary-item><button type=button class="usa-accordion__button usa-nav__link" aria-expanded=false aria-controls=section-categories><span>Categories</span></button><ul id=section-categories class=usa-nav__submenu><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/categories/water-data>water data</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/categories/data-science>data science</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/categories/water-data-for-the-nation>water data for the nation</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/categories/data-visualization>data visualization</a></li></ul></li><li class=usa-nav__primary-item><button type=button class="usa-accordion__button usa-nav__link" aria-expanded=false aria-controls=section-tags><span>Tags</span></button><ul id=section-tags class=usa-nav__submenu><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/water-data-for-the-nation>water data for the nation</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/nextgen>nextgen</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/r>r</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/monitoring-location-pages>monitoring location pages</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/api>api</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/dataretrieval>dataretrieval</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/decommission>decommission</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/streamgage>streamgage</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/vizlab>vizlab</a></li><li class=usa-nav__submenu-item><a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/beyond-basic-r>beyond basic r</a></li></ul></li></ul><div class=usa-nav__secondary><form action=/blog/search method=GET data-search-index=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/index.json class="usa-search usa-search--small" role=search><label class=usa-sr-only for=search-query>Search NOW</label>
<input class=usa-input id=search-query type=search name=q>
<button class=usa-button type=submit>
<img src=/blog/wdfn-viz/img/usa-icons-bg/search--white.svg class=usa-search__submit-icon alt=Search></button></form></div></div></nav></header><div class=grid-col-fill><main id=main-content role=main class=main-content><article class="single grid-container-desktop"><h1 class="text-ls-neg-2 padding-bottom-0 margin-bottom-0">Intentional degradations to WaterServices ahead of final decommissioning</h1><h3 class=text-normal>In order to alert automated users of WaterServices, we will intentionally slow down requests and perform two scheduled outages before permanently decommissioning the services in February 2027.</h3><div class="grid-row display-flex flex-justify border-y padding-y-1"><div><span class="display-block text-uppercase">Date Posted</span>
<span class=text-bold>September 18, 2026</span>
<span class="display-block text-uppercase margin-top-1">Last Updated</span>
<span class=text-bold>September 18, 2026</span></div><div><span class="display-block text-uppercase">Author</span>
<span class=text-bold>Michael Mahoney</span><br><a href=mailto:wdfn@usgs.gov class=text-no-underline target=blank><i class="fas fa-envelope-square text-primary-darker social-icon"></i></a></div><div><span class="display-block text-uppercase">Reading Time</span>
<span class=text-bold>2 minutes</span>
<span class="display-block text-uppercase margin-top-1">Share</span>
<a href="http://www.facebook.com/sharer.php?src=bm&u=https%3a%2f%2fwaterdata.usgs.gov%2fblog%2fwdfn-waterservices-degradation%2f&t=Intentional%20degradations%20to%20WaterServices%20ahead%20of%20final%20decommissioning" class="text-no-underline margin-right-1" onclick='return window.open(this.href,"PCwindow","width=550, height=350, menubar=no, toolbar=no, scrollbars=yes"),!1'><i class="fab fa-facebook text-primary-darker social-icon" aria-hidden=true></i>
</a><a href="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?url=https%3a%2f%2fwaterdata.usgs.gov%2fblog%2fwdfn-waterservices-degradation%2f&text=Intentional%20degradations%20to%20WaterServices%20ahead%20of%20final%20decommissioning&tw_p=tweetbutton" class="text-no-underline margin-right-1" rel=nofollow target=_blank><i class="fab fa-twitter text-primary-darker social-icon" aria-hidden=true></i>
</a><a href="https://www.reddit.com/submit?url=https%3a%2f%2fwaterdata.usgs.gov%2fblog%2fwdfn-waterservices-degradation%2f&title=Intentional%20degradations%20to%20WaterServices%20ahead%20of%20final%20decommissioning" class=text-no-underline onclick='return window.open(this.href,"PCwindow","width=550, height=350, menubar=no, toolbar=no, scrollbars=yes"),!1'><i class="fab fa-reddit-alien text-primary-darker social-icon" aria-hidden=true></i></a></div></div><div style=padding:5px;background-color:#c0bdd6><h2 style=margin:10px>Public USGS Webinar: NWISWeb Decommissioning Campaign 3</h2><p style=margin:10px>NWISWeb launched real-time data pages in 1995 and has hosted more than 7 million annual unique visitors, billions of successful page requests, and terabytes of data delivered. After several years of modernization, we are beginning the final decommissioning or turning off of legacy NWISWeb webpages. This means that pages that you may have relied on for years are going away.<br><br>This webinar will share information on NWISWeb Decommission Campaign 3, which will retire all remaining NWISWeb pages and WaterServices. Campaign 3 is expected to be ongoing from November 2026 through February 2027.<br><br></p><p style=margin:10px;font-size:20px;font-weight:700>Join the External Webinar on October 1, 2026 at 1pm Central using <a href="https://teams.microsoft.com/l/meetup-join/19%3ameeting_OGZlMTViMGMtOWE0ZC00ZDdhLWExZTMtNzQ3YjRlNWI1Njhk%40thread.v2/0?context=%7b%22Tid%22%3a%220693b5ba-4b18-4d7b-9341-f32f400a5494%22%2c%22Oid%22%3a%226656023f-c3b2-403a-8d36-b460a49b33b8%22%7d">this link</a>.</p></div><p>As <a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/api-waterservices-decom/ target=_blank>previously announced</a>, we have released modernized <a href=https://api.waterdata.usgs.gov target=_blank>Water Data APIs</a> which will supersede the WaterServices family of APIs. <strong>WaterServices will be decommissioned on February 22nd, 2027.</strong></p><p>We are using multiple avenues to advertise this decommissioning, including placing banners on waterservices.usgs.gov, writing public announcements, sending communications via <a href=https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOIGS/signup/35025 target=_blank>the WDFN newsletter</a>, and hosting recorded webinars (see announcement above) with time for Q&amp;A about this change and the migration efforts needed to move to the new APIs. However, many users of WaterServices only interact with the services through automated programmatic data downloads and may not see any of these announcements.</p><p>As such, we will be implementing intentional service degradations and outages on WaterServices ahead of its final decommissioning to alert these users to the necessary migrations to their code. Specifically, we will make the following changes:</p><ul><li>On November 16th, 2026, we will add a 2 second delay to all requests made to WaterServices.</li><li>On January 11th, 2027, we will increase this delay to 10 seconds per request.</li><li>On January 25th, 2027, we will increase this delay to 30 seconds per request.</li><li>On January 27th, 2027, we will redirect all requests to waterservices.usgs.gov to this blog post for approximately 24 hours. We will restore regular service on January 28th, 2027.</li><li>On February 1st, 2027, we will increase the delay to 60 seconds per request.</li><li>On February 15th, 2027, we will redirect all requests to waterservices.usgs.gov to this blog post for approximately 48 hours. We will restore regular service on February 17th, 2027.</li><li>On February 22nd, 2027, we will redirect all requests to waterservices.usgs.gov to our <a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/api-waterservices-decom/ target=_blank>previous decommissioning blog post</a>.</li></ul><p>The timing and length of these delays may be adjusted as necessary. We will not implement the redirects before the dates listed. We do not anticipate delaying the February 22nd decommissioning date.</p><p>Users will need to migrate to the new Water Data APIs before November 16th, 2026, to avoid any impact. More information about the new APIs can be found <a href=https://api.waterdata.usgs.gov/docs/ogcapi/ target=_blank>in our documentation</a>, which includes <a href=https://api.waterdata.usgs.gov/docs/ogcapi/migration/ target=_blank>a migration guide</a> for updating code to use the new services.</p><p>Users of the dataRetrieval packages for R and Python will additionally need to update their code to use the new <code>read_waterdata</code> functions (in R) or <code>waterdata</code> module (in Python).</p><p>We understand that change is hard, and some of these changes might feel sudden. We’re here to help. We have staff ready to help you make the transition should you need it. Please reach out to us at <a href=mailto:wdfn@usgs.gov>wdfn@usgs.gov</a> with any questions.</p><div class="grid-row border-y display-flex flex-align-center padding-y-1"><div class="display-flex flex-12"><div class=taxo-categories><h3 class=margin-y-0>Categories:</h3><ul class="usa-list usa-list--unstyled margin-right-1"><li class="display-inline-block margin-right-05"><a class="usa-tag text-no-underline" href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/categories/water-data/ data-taxonomy-term=water-data><span>Water Data</span></a></li><li class="display-inline-block margin-right-05"><a class="usa-tag text-no-underline" href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/categories/water-data-for-the-nation/ data-taxonomy-term=water-data-for-the-nation><span>Water Data for the Nation</span></a></li></ul></div><div class=taxo-tags><h3 class=margin-y-0>Tags:</h3><ul class="usa-list usa-list--unstyled margin-right-1"><li class="display-inline-block margin-right-05"><a class="usa-tag text-no-underline" href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/water-data-for-the-nation/ data-taxonomy-term=water-data-for-the-nation><span>Water Data for the Nation</span></a></li><li class="display-inline-block margin-right-05"><a class="usa-tag text-no-underline" href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/api/ data-taxonomy-term=api><span>API</span></a></li><li class="display-inline-block margin-right-05"><a class="usa-tag text-no-underline" href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/water-services/ data-taxonomy-term=water-services><span>Water Services</span></a></li><li class="display-inline-block margin-right-05"><a class="usa-tag text-no-underline" href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/waterservices/ data-taxonomy-term=waterservices><span>WaterServices</span></a></li><li class="display-inline-block margin-right-05"><a class="usa-tag text-no-underline" href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/tags/decommissioning/ data-taxonomy-term=decommissioning><span>Decommissioning</span></a></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="grid-row flex-justify-end flex-align-center"><h3 class=margin-right-1>Share:</h3><a href="http://www.facebook.com/sharer.php?src=bm&u=https%3a%2f%2fwaterdata.usgs.gov%2fblog%2fwdfn-waterservices-degradation%2f&t=Intentional%20degradations%20to%20WaterServices%20ahead%20of%20final%20decommissioning" class="text-no-underline margin-right-1" onclick='return window.open(this.href,"PCwindow","width=550, height=350, menubar=no, toolbar=no, scrollbars=yes"),!1'><i class="fab fa-facebook text-primary-darker social-icon" aria-hidden=true></i>
</a><a href="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?url=https%3a%2f%2fwaterdata.usgs.gov%2fblog%2fwdfn-waterservices-degradation%2f&text=Intentional%20degradations%20to%20WaterServices%20ahead%20of%20final%20decommissioning&tw_p=tweetbutton" class="text-no-underline margin-right-1" rel=nofollow target=_blank><i class="fab fa-twitter text-primary-darker social-icon" aria-hidden=true></i>
</a><a href="https://www.reddit.com/submit?url=https%3a%2f%2fwaterdata.usgs.gov%2fblog%2fwdfn-waterservices-degradation%2f&title=Intentional%20degradations%20to%20WaterServices%20ahead%20of%20final%20decommissioning" class=text-no-underline onclick='return window.open(this.href,"PCwindow","width=550, height=350, menubar=no, toolbar=no, scrollbars=yes"),!1'><i class="fab fa-reddit-alien text-primary-darker social-icon" aria-hidden=true></i></a></div><section class=margin-top-2><h2 class=text-uppercase>Related Posts</h2><ul class=usa-card-group><li class="desktop:grid-col-6 usa-card"><div class=usa-card__container><div class=usa-card__header><h2 class=usa-card__heading>Announcing V1 of the WDFN APIs</h2></div><div class=usa-card__body><p class=margin-y-0>September 4, 2026</p><p><div style=padding:5px;background-color:#c0bdd6><h2 style=margin:10px>Public USGS Webinar: NWISWeb Decommissioning Campaign 3</h2><p style=margin:10px>NWISWeb launched real-time data pages in 1995 and has hosted more than 7 million annual unique visitors, billions of successful page requests, and terabytes of data delivered. After several years of modernization, we are beginning the final decommissioning or turning off of legacy NWISWeb webpages. This means that pages that you may have relied on for years are going away.<br><br>This webinar will share information on NWISWeb Decommission Campaign 3, which will retire all remaining NWISWeb pages and WaterServices. Campaign 3 is expected to be ongoing from November 2026 through February 2027.<br><br></p></p></div><div class=usa-card__footer><a href=/blog/api-v1-release/ class=usa-button>Read More...</a></div></div></li><li class="desktop:grid-col-6 usa-card"><div class=usa-card__container><div class=usa-card__header><h2 class=usa-card__heading>What's new with WDFN APIs - Summer 2026 Edition</h2></div><div class=usa-card__body><p class=margin-y-0>June 18, 2026</p><p><div style=padding:5px;background-color:#c0bdd6><h2 style=margin:10px>Public USGS Webinar: NWISWeb Decommissioning Campaign 3</h2><p style=margin:10px>NWISWeb launched real-time data pages in 1995 and has hosted more than 7 million annual unique visitors, billions of successful page requests, and terabytes of data delivered. After several years of modernization, we are beginning the final decommissioning or turning off of legacy NWISWeb webpages. This means that pages that you may have relied on for years are going away.<br><br>This webinar will share information on NWISWeb Decommission Campaign 3, which will retire all remaining NWISWeb pages and WaterServices. Campaign 3 is expected to be ongoing from November 2026 through February 2027.<br><br></p></p></div><div class=usa-card__footer><a href=/blog/api-updates-2026/ class=usa-button>Read More...</a></div></div></li><li class="desktop:grid-col-6 usa-card"><div class=usa-card__container><div class=usa-card__header><h2 class=usa-card__heading>Big changes to USGS Water Data</h2></div><div class=usa-card__body><p class=margin-y-0>May 28, 2025</p><p><div style=padding:5px;background-color:#c0bdd6><h2 style=margin:10px>Public USGS Webinar: NWISWeb Decommissioning Campaign 3</h2><p style=margin:10px>NWISWeb launched real-time data pages in 1995 and has hosted more than 7 million annual unique visitors, billions of successful page requests, and terabytes of data delivered. After several years of modernization, we are beginning the final decommissioning or turning off of legacy NWISWeb webpages. This means that pages that you may have relied on for years are going away.<br><br>This webinar will share information on NWISWeb Decommission Campaign 3, which will retire all remaining NWISWeb pages and WaterServices. Campaign 3 is expected to be ongoing from November 2026 through February 2027.<br><br></p></p></div><div class=usa-card__footer><a href=/blog/wdfn-updates-2025/ class=usa-button>Read More...</a></div></div></li><li class="desktop:grid-col-6 usa-card"><div class=usa-card__container><div class=usa-card__header><h2 class=usa-card__heading>What's new with WDFN APIs?</h2></div><div class=usa-card__body><p class=margin-y-0>May 21, 2025</p><p><style>.code-toolbar{max-height:400px;overflow:scroll}</style><div style=padding:5px;background-color:#e1f3f8><h2 style=margin:10px>USGS Water Data APIs Homepage and Informational Webinar are available!</h2><p style=margin:10px>We have continued to modernize Water Data APIs. Keep visiting this blog for more updates</p></p></div><div class=usa-card__footer><a href=/blog/api-whats-new-wdfn-apis/ class=usa-button>Read More...</a></div></div></li><li class="desktop:grid-col-6 usa-card"><div class=usa-card__container><div class=usa-card__header><h2 class=usa-card__heading>Summer 2024 Impacts to WaterServices</h2></div><div class=usa-card__body><p class=margin-y-0>July 3, 2024</p><p><div style=padding:5px;background-color:#e1f3f8><h2 style=margin:10px>WaterServices APIs are being decommissioned in 2027!</h2><p style=margin:10px>We have released modernized Water Data APIs which will supersede the WaterServices family of APIs. Users will need to migrate their applications to use these new services in order to retain uninterrupted access to USGS water data going forward. Read this <a href=https://waterdata.usgs.gov/blog/api-waterservices-decom>blog for more information</a>.</p></p></div><div class=usa-card__footer><a href=/blog/wdfn-waterservices-2024/ class=usa-button>Read More...</a></div></div></li></ul></section></div></main></div><footer class="usa-footer usa-footer--slim" role=contentinfo><nav class=usgs-footer-container aria-label="Footer Navigation"><div class=usgs-footer-nav><a class=usgs-footer-link href=https://www.doi.gov/privacy>DOI Privacy Policy</a> |
